text:
Tabby creates financial freedom in the way people shop, earn and save by reshaping their relationship with money. Over 15 million users choose Tabby to stay in control of their spending and make the most out of their money.
The company’s flagship offering allows shoppers to split their payments online and in-store with no interest or fees. Over 40,000 global brands and small businesses, including Amazon, Noon, IKEA, and SHEIN use Tabby to accelerate growth and gain loyal customers by offering easy and flexible payments online and in stores.

Tabby generates over $10 billion in annual transaction volume for its partner brands and is the highest-rated, most-reviewed, largest, and fastest-growing FinTech in the GCC region.

Tabby launched in 2019 and has since raised +$1 billion in equity and debt funding from global and regional investors, and is now valued at $6.5 billion.

About the role:

This is a hybrid role that combines hands-on operational support, process ownership and incident management. You'll be the link between support, engineering and business teams, making sure issues are identified, prioritised and resolved quickly.
Incident management is one of the core areas of the role. Tabby is a 24/7 payments business, so incidents are a natural part of the job. You'll be involved in handling them from first alert to post-mortem, and take part in an on-call rotation that occasionally includes out-of-hours alerts.

Key responsibilities:

Incident management

Respond to alerts and incidents: triage, assess impact and escalate to the right teams;

Coordinate resolution and keep stakeholders informed;

Take part in the on-call rotation;

Contribute to post-mortems and follow up on action items.

Operational support

Handle requests from the support team and colleagues;

Investigate technical issues using logs, metrics and SQL, identify bugs and create clear tasks for development teams;

Maintain runbooks and documentation for L1 and L2 teams.

Process & tooling

Improve support and incident management processes;

Automate routine tasks and contribute to internal tools (BackOffice, alerting);

Explore and implement AI tools and LLM-based solutions to speed up request handling, incident triage and documentation (e.g. auto-categorisation, summarisation, knowledge-base assistants).

What You'll Bring:

Experience in service desk, production support or a similar operational role;

Hands-on experience with incident management, or a strong interest in it;

Ability to stay structured and communicate clearly when things break;

Strong soft skills: ownership, proactivity, high level of autonomy;

Experience with monitoring and logging tools (Datadog, Grafana, Kibana);

Experience writing simple SQL queries;

Experience working with Jira;

English at a level sufficient for written communication and reading technical documentation (B2+).

Nice to have:

Experience implementing AI / LLM tools in support or operational processes (chatbots, AI agents, workflow automation, prompt engineering);

Experience with Google Cloud;

Experience with Google Apps Script;

Scripting skills (Bash, Python, Go);

Understanding of ITIL processes;

Jira administration experience.

This role might not be for you if:

You're looking for a stable schedule with no out-of-hours work;

You find frequent multitasking and context switching stressful;

You prefer long, deep-focus tasks over a fast-paced operational environment.

What we offer:

Full-time B2B contract

Fully remote setup, work from anywhere in Europe

Up to 20% tax allowance

22 paid leave days annually

Additional compensation for on-call duty

Stock options (ESOP) in a fast-scaling, pre-IPO company

Flexi benefits you can use for wellness, travel, or learning

Real ownership and fast growth in incident and operations management

Room to experiment with AI and modern tooling to shape how our operations work

Work alongside a high-performing, international engineering team in a global fintech unicorn

